# the live call is instantiated; the one behind `const if (false)` is not. RAST shows instances
# as `function name -> type<concrete>` beside the template's `type<T>`. CHECK-NOT is scoped
# between neighbours, so one before the keep instance and one after covers the whole dump

--- OUT --->
2
--- RAST --->
CHECK: function poison -> type<T>
CHECK: function keep -> type<T>
CHECK-NOT: function poison -> type<int32>
CHECK: function keep -> type<int32>
CHECK-NOT: function poison -> type<int32>
